# Lines Silica prints in place of Apple's, accepted.
#
# Scaling an image up with the default interpolation: Apple's filter keeps
# each pixel's color to within a couple of pixels of its neighbors, Cairo's
# bilinear filter blends across the whole pixel. With kCGInterpolationNone
# both take the nearest pixel, and agree.
image top left: 249 5 0 255
image bottom left: 13 5 247 255
image bottom right: 247 255 247 255
#
# A color made with CGColorCreateGenericRGB: Apple converts it from the
# Generic RGB space to the context's, which moves pure blue toward green.
# Silica has no color management: Generic RGB is sRGB.
shadow: 0 0 256 256
